    "body": "Fixes #43580\n\n## Motivation\n\n`DeepseekV2Model.forward` exports the stage output through `residual_batch.to_pp()` before checking whether a non-idle batch has rows that require DSA top-k indices. A residual-stream output may still be represented locally by an opaque `OwedOutput`, so reading `hidden_states.shape` after export raises `AttributeError` during the PP handoff.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Read the row count from the exported `proxy_tensors[\"hidden_states\"]` tensor.\n- Use the same exported tensor when allocating empty top-k indices for the zero-row case, preserving its device and the existing `torch.int32` shape contract.\n- Add a CPU regression that runs the real `DeepseekV2Model.forward` PP branch with an `OwedOutput`, exercises `residual_batch.to_pp()` / `ResidualStream.export()` for declared-sum and deferred-finalize outputs, and covers nonempty/empty rows.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Baseline: the new real-forward regression raises the reported `AttributeError: OwedOutput has no attribute shape` before this fix.\n- `pytest test/registered/unit/models/test_deepseek_pp_mtp_embedding.py -q -s` (CPU-only): 5 passed, 18 environment/deprecation warnings.\n- Independent root rerun after rebasing to `1809335`: 5 passed. The native-filesystem Python source copy used for faster imports was SHA-256 verified against the submitted production file; the test file was loaded directly from the submitted worktree.\n- `pre-commit run --files python/sglang/srt/models/deepseek_v2.py test/registered/unit/models/test_deepseek_pp_mtp_embedding.py`: all applicable hooks passed.\n- `pre-commit run --all-files` was attempted, but not green: baseline symlink blobs trigger EOF normalization and the local Windows Cargo installation lacks nightly/fmt/clippy support. Only the generated baseline changes were restored; no unrelated code was changed to make checks pass.\n\nNo GPU/model-load or throughput benchmark was run. The change is confined to PP metadata bookkeeping and empty-index allocation; the focused test uses CPU tensors and mocks only the parallel reduction/finalization work.\n\nDuplicate check: no open PR implements this OwedOutput handoff fix. Numeric issue search also returns unrelated NPU prefix-cache PR #30451; it does not address these accesses. Existing frontend-stream PR #43651 is independent and unchanged.\n\nAI disclosure: investigated, implemented and tested with OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Luna worker and independent root audit). Local CPU evidence does not establish GPU end-to-end validation.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo end-to-end GPU accuracy evaluation was run. The change does not alter layer computation or the hidden-state values; maintainers can decide whether a model-level GPU run is needed before merge.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run; this patch does not change a compute kernel or introduce a throughput optimization.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format/lint checks for changed files.\n- [x] Focused CPU regression test.\n- [ ] Full repository CI and GPU/model validation.\n- [ ] Codeowner and Merge Oncall review.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38235428529](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38235428529)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38235428219](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38235428219)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38235428317](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38235428317)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
